.SH NAME
.PP
http_sendfield - sends HTTP field to the peer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
#include <libdill.h>

int http_sendfield(
    int s,
    const char* name,
    const char* value,
    int64_t deadline);
\f[R]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\f[B]WARNING: This is experimental functionality and the API may change
in the future.\f[R]
.PP
HTTP is an application-level protocol described in RFC 7230.
This implementation handles only the request/response exchange.
Whatever comes after that must be handled by a different protocol.
.PP
This function sends an HTTP field, i.e.
a name/value pair, to the peer.
For example, if name is \f[B]Host\f[R] and resource is
\f[B]www.example.org\f[R] the line sent will look like this:
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
Host: www.example.org
\f[R]
.fi
.PP
After sending the last field of HTTP request don\[aq]t forget to call
\f[B]http_done\f[R] on the socket.
It will send an empty line to the server to let it know that the request
is finished and it should start processing it.
.PP
\f[B]s\f[R]: HTTP socket handle.
.PP
\f[B]name\f[R]: Name of the field.
.PP
\f[B]value\f[R]: Value of the field.
.PP
\f[B]deadline\f[R]: A point in time when the operation should time out,
in milliseconds.
Use the \f[B]now\f[R] function to get your current point in time.
0 means immediate timeout, i.e., perform the operation if possible or
return without blocking if not.
-1 means no deadline, i.e., the call will block forever if the operation
cannot be performed.
.PP
This function is not available if libdill is compiled with
\f[B]--disable-sockets\f[R] option.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
In case of success the function returns 0.
In case of error it returns -1 and sets \f[B]errno\f[R] to one of the
values below.
.SH ERRORS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]EBADF\f[R]: Invalid handle.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]ECANCELED\f[R]: Current coroutine was canceled.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]ECONNRESET\f[R]: Broken connection.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]EINVAL\f[R]: Invalid argument.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]ENOTSUP\f[R]: The handle does not support this operation.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]EPROTO\f[R]: The value is empty or contains only spaces.
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]ETIMEDOUT\f[R]: Deadline was reached.
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
int s = tcp_connect(&addr, -1);
s = http_attach(s);
http_sendrequest(s, \[dq]GET\[dq], \[dq]/\[dq], -1);
http_sendfield(s, \[dq]Host\[dq], \[dq]www.example.org\[dq], -1);
http_done(s, -1);
char reason[256];
http_recvstatus(s, reason, sizeof(reason), -1);
while(1) {
    char name[256];
    char value[256];
    int rc = http_recvfield(s, name, sizeof(name), value, sizeof(value), -1);
